{"repositoryId":735339964,"availability":"available","full":"DanielLin0516/SUBWAY-SURFERS","name":"SUBWAY-SURFERS","description":"Threejs,Subway-surfers","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":46,"forks":36,"created":"2023-12-24T14:55:31Z","updated":"2026-10-14T11:39:13Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://subway-surfers-flax.vercel.app","topics":["subway-surfers","threejs"],"demo":"https://subway-surfers-flax.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:32.438Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:32.438Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:32.438Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T03:00:32.438Z","stars":46,"forks":36}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A three-lane endless runner made with three.js and TypeScript.","The online version at is still the old version until this branch is deployed."],"features":["Lane-based collision. Each obstacle is an interval along the track, across its lane, and in height; the runner is a small box. Results are exact and repeatable. Forgiving edges: clipping a corner while leaving a lane is…","Obstacles: low barriers (jump), hurdles (jump or roll), overhead gates (roll), trains (dodge, or run up a ramp and along the roofs), and oncoming trains with blinking headlights, a light band on the track, a horn and a…","Feel: fast eased lane changes (0.15 s), lane changes in the air, jump buffer (a jump pressed just before landing still happens), coyote time, fast fall, jump out of a roll, speed rising slowly from 12 to 27 m/s.","Endless map built in 100 m chunks. Every chunk is checked with a path search before it is used, so there is always a way through; difficulty grows with distance. Coins are laid along that way.","Coins, score multiplier (rises every 800 m), best score and coin bank saved in localStorage."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/DanielLin0516/SUBWAY-SURFERS/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"539086e51ab5d4f4654d2db97f80abacdc8